# Frontend Review Standards

## State Management (Zustand / appStore.ts)

- All state mutations go through `actions.ts` helpers. **Never** call `useAppStore.getState().updateData()` directly from a component.
- Use the typed selectors exported from `appStore.ts` (e.g. `useSettings`, `useTeamMembers`). Never call `useAppStore(state => state.data.X)` inline in a component for objects — use `useShallow` to prevent infinite re-render loops (React 19 / `useSyncExternalStore`).
- UI-only state (modals open, local form values) must stay in component `useState` — do not hoist it into the Zustand store.
- `getCurrentState()` merges scenario data on every call. Avoid calling it in render-hot paths; use `useCurrentState()` selector instead.

## Component Patterns

- Prefer small, focused components. A component over ~200 lines is a signal to extract sub-components or a custom hook.
- Custom hooks go in `hooks/`. If a piece of logic is used in two or more components, extract it.
- Never use inline arrow functions as event handlers on elements that re-render frequently (e.g. Gantt rows). Use `useCallback`.
- The dual IT/BIZ track model is **non-negotiable**. Every feature that displays team members or assignments must render both tracks.

## Gantt / Timeline Rules

- Gantt rows must **never** have `overflow: hidden` — it hides the clip-left/clip-right pseudo-element arrows.
- Bar colours are defined in `GanttBar.*` in `frontend/src/theme/tokens.ts`. The `BAR` map in `JiraGantt.tsx` must reference `tokens.ts` — do not add bare hex literals there.
- `barLayout()` returns values in the range `0.0–1.0`; apply as `${value * 100}%` inline styles. Do not convert to pixels.
- Date resolution uses a three-pass fallback (Jira date → sprint object dates → sprint name lookup). All three passes must remain intact.

## Styling

- Use Tailwind utility classes first. Only add custom CSS in `index.css` for things Tailwind cannot express (e.g. Gantt pseudo-elements, scrollbar styles).
- Colours must use `sana-*`, `util-*`, or `biz-*` Tailwind token names, or named exports from `frontend/src/theme/tokens.ts` for inline styles. **Never hardcode hex values in component files.**
- The `mw-*` Tailwind namespace is legacy — do not use it in new code. Prefer `sana-teal` over `mw-primary`, `sana-text` over `mw-dark`, etc.
- Dark mode is architecturally wired but **deferred**. Do NOT add new `dark:` Tailwind variant classes. The toggle exists in the sidebar but has no visual effect until dark mode is un-deferred.
- Do not use `document.body.classList` or `document.documentElement` directly in components for theme toggling.

## UX / Accessibility

- Every interactive element must have a visible focus ring (`focus:ring-2 focus:ring-sana-teal`).
- Modal dialogs must trap focus and close on `Escape`. Use the `Modal` primitive from `components/ui/`.
- Loading states must show a skeleton or spinner — never a blank area. Use the `ProgressBar` or a `div animate-pulse` skeleton.
- Error states must offer a recovery action (retry button, dismiss). Do not show raw error messages from Supabase or Jira to the user.
- Keyboard navigation: views 1–6 are bound to number keys; `Ctrl+K` opens the command palette. Do not shadow these shortcuts in new components.

## TypeScript

- All TypeScript interfaces are defined in `types/index.ts` — the single source of truth. Do not create local interface definitions that duplicate or partially mirror those in `types/`.
- Avoid `as unknown as X` casts. If a cast is truly necessary, add a comment explaining why.
- Prefer `type` over `interface` for union/intersection types; use `interface` for object shapes that may be extended.

## Performance

- `JiraGantt.tsx` and `JiraHierarchyTree.tsx` render potentially hundreds of rows. Memoize row data with `useMemo`; memoize callbacks with `useCallback`.
- Avoid deriving computed data (capacity totals, rollup dates) inside render. Move derivations to `useMemo` or utility functions.
- Do not add new synchronous `localStorage.getItem` calls in render paths — they block the main thread.

## Testing (future standard)

- There is currently no test coverage. When adding tests:
  - Unit tests for utils (`sprints.ts`, `capacity.ts`, `confidence.ts`) with Vitest.
  - Integration tests for `supabaseSync.ts` against a local Supabase instance.
  - E2E tests for critical flows (login, Jira sync, scenario creation) with Playwright.
